885:
Nonconforming uses of land shall be discontinued within three years from the date this Ordinance becomes effective, or within three years from the date the use becomes nonconforming, whichever is later, in the following situations;
1. Where no buildings are used in connection with the principal use;
2. Where the only buildings used are accessory or incidental to the principal use;
3. Where the use is maintained in connection with a building originally constructed for a conforming use;
4. Outdoor advertising signs;
5. Movable signs and any free-standing signs closer than ten feet to any street right-of-way and signs attached to trees or utility poles.
